   "widgets_values": [
    "VFX element -> animated frames (animator lane)\n\nCheckpoint: sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors\nLoRA: pixel-art-xl.safetensors (weight 1.0; do NOT put 'pixel art' in the prompt)\nSampler: dpmpp_2m + karras, 25 steps, CFG 5, 1024x1024, fixed seed for a repeatable set\n\nThis graph makes ONE high-detail element frame on a flat keyable backdrop.\n`tools/gen_vfx_sheet.py` keys the backdrop, downscales to a small pixel size,\nthen derives the 8-frame animation (expand / billow / rise / spin) so the\nsequence is deterministic and the diffusion model only has to draw the shape\nwell once. That is much more reliable than asking SDXL for a sprite sheet.\n\nRun (ComfyUI at 127.0.0.1:8188):\n  python tools/gen_vfx_sheet.py --kind flare --seed 4201\n  python tools/gen_vfx_sheet.py --kind smoke --seed 4202\n  python tools/gen_vfx_sheet.py --kind ember --seed 4203\n\nThen check assets/vfx/preview.png and re-run the game. The VFX module prefers\nthese authored sheets automatically; the procedural art in\ntools/make_vfx_art.py stays as the fallback.\n\nFLARE: keep the core small and the sparks as separate hard wedges. The script expands and fades them; a wide soft cloud reads as smoke and loses the impact read."
   ]
  },
